WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.244 --> 00:00:01.341
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.341 --> 00:00:04.721
Today's message is focus on the journey.

00:00:04.721 --> 00:00:06.194
Over to you, Jessie J.

00:00:06.194 --> 00:00:08.562
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.562 --> 00:00:11.195
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.195 --> 00:00:13.901
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:17.868
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:19.035
- I don't ever

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.601
disregard the fact that
however hard you work,

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:26.024
it doesn't always guarantee
it's going to happen.

00:00:26.024 --> 00:00:28.820
That's the thing that
you have to just believe.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:29.906
If you don't believe in you,

00:00:29.906 --> 00:00:32.587
no one else will even
bother to look at you.

00:00:32.587 --> 00:00:35.834
I shoved myself on any
open mics, any gigs.

00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:37.229
The amount of stuff.

00:00:37.229 --> 00:00:39.675
I've probably done, even up to now,

00:00:39.675 --> 00:00:42.172
80, 90% of all my gigs for free.

00:00:42.172 --> 00:00:43.791
Surround yourself with
people that you can trust.

00:00:43.791 --> 00:00:46.971
Surround yourself with
people that let you be you.

00:00:46.971 --> 00:00:49.759
Compromise, but don't ever

00:00:49.759 --> 00:00:52.377
lose what makes you you.

00:00:52.377 --> 00:00:54.253
Write from the heart.

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:55.219
Stay happy.

00:00:55.219 --> 00:00:56.052
Always remember,

00:00:56.052 --> 00:00:58.061
there's always someone worse off than you

00:00:58.061 --> 00:00:58.894
and there's always someone

00:00:58.894 --> 00:01:00.050
that's working harder than you as well.

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:01.639
When you're asleep,
there's someone grafting.

00:01:01.639 --> 00:01:02.732
That's what you have to remember as well,

00:01:02.732 --> 00:01:04.910
that for every 10 CD's you send off

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:06.893
there's someone sending off 100.

00:01:06.893 --> 00:01:08.416
Just get yourself out
there as much as you can,

00:01:08.416 --> 00:01:09.727
and film everything.

00:01:09.727 --> 00:01:11.076
That's one thing I've learned.

00:01:11.076 --> 00:01:13.410
I'm glad that I did footage for music.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:14.539
People say to me,

00:01:14.539 --> 00:01:15.422
"You've copied so-and-so.

00:01:15.422 --> 00:01:16.283
"You've done this, you've done that."

00:01:16.283 --> 00:01:17.256
I'm like, "Go on YouTube.

00:01:17.256 --> 00:01:18.089
"Five years ago I was singing

00:01:18.089 --> 00:01:19.888
"the same songs with the same haircut."

00:01:19.888 --> 00:01:21.558
You've got to have fun as well.

00:01:21.558 --> 00:01:22.443
Write it down.

00:01:22.443 --> 00:01:24.964
Make sure you write it
down, take pictures.

00:01:24.964 --> 00:01:26.841
Make sure it's a journey.

00:01:26.841 --> 00:01:30.076
The journey is way more
important than where you end up.

00:01:30.076 --> 00:01:31.205
That's what you have to remember.

00:01:31.205 --> 00:01:33.707
- One of the most popular
questions I get asked is,

00:01:33.707 --> 00:01:35.023
"How will I know when I've reached

00:01:35.023 --> 00:01:37.067
"one billion entrepreneurs?"

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:38.379
My big goal,

00:01:38.379 --> 00:01:40.672
my big vision, mission, what I want to do,

00:01:40.672 --> 00:01:42.208
I want to reach a billion entrepreneurs.

00:01:42.208 --> 00:01:43.712
I want to know that I'm having

00:01:43.712 --> 00:01:45.456
that kind of impact and put out

00:01:45.456 --> 00:01:48.173
content and create amazing things

00:01:48.173 --> 00:01:50.884
for a ton of entrepreneurs.

00:01:50.884 --> 00:01:51.717
I get people asking,

00:01:51.717 --> 00:01:53.211
"Well, how will you know

00:01:53.211 --> 00:01:54.977
"when you hit a billion entrepreneurs?

00:01:54.977 --> 00:01:55.810
"I don't think there's even

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:57.934
"a billion entrepreneurs in the world."

00:01:57.934 --> 00:01:59.442
You're missing the point.

00:01:59.442 --> 00:02:01.569
I don't actually have a way to track

00:02:01.569 --> 00:02:03.461
if I'm hitting a billion entrepreneurs,

00:02:03.461 --> 00:02:04.940
and I don't care about it

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:07.327
because I'm not focused on the goal.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:09.086
I'm focused on the journey.

00:02:09.086 --> 00:02:11.800
What it does is make sure that

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.812
it aligns me to think about big projects.

00:02:14.812 --> 00:02:17.487
Anything that I'm spending
significant time on

00:02:17.487 --> 00:02:19.432
I want to make sure has the ability

00:02:19.432 --> 00:02:21.172
to reach a lot of people.

00:02:21.172 --> 00:02:22.759
I'm making YouTube videos because

00:02:22.759 --> 00:02:24.947
it can spread and reach a lot of people.

00:02:24.947 --> 00:02:26.636
When I started to write my book,

00:02:26.636 --> 00:02:28.976
I wanted to do it with a big publisher,

00:02:28.976 --> 00:02:30.360
not just self-publish.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:33.004
Even though self-publishing
can make me a lot more money,

00:02:33.004 --> 00:02:33.949
I went with a big publisher

00:02:33.949 --> 00:02:36.157
because I wanted to try to get more reach.

00:02:36.157 --> 00:02:37.836
It's the reason why I don't do

00:02:37.836 --> 00:02:40.224
business coaching and
one-on-one consulting.

00:02:40.224 --> 00:02:42.595
Although it could be really meaningful

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.810
and great to have the
one-on-one connection,

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:46.734
I want to do things on a bigger scale.

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:49.884
What that big goal allows me to do

00:02:49.884 --> 00:02:52.930
is focus my efforts on the right projects.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:55.615
I don't actually care about hitting

00:02:55.615 --> 00:02:57.307
a billion entrepreneurs.

00:02:57.307 --> 00:02:59.533
Just like if I say, "My next
goal on the YouTube channel

00:02:59.533 --> 00:03:01.454
"is I want to hit a million subscribers."

00:03:01.454 --> 00:03:03.066
It's amazing, it's great.

00:03:03.066 --> 00:03:04.590
You get a play button.

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:07.422
We might have another celebration.

00:03:07.422 --> 00:03:09.748
As soon as I hit a goal,

00:03:09.748 --> 00:03:11.052
I don't really celebrate.

00:03:11.052 --> 00:03:13.975
I feel like I need to celebrate
more because, my team,

00:03:13.975 --> 00:03:16.799
it's a good thing to do
kind of for team building.

00:03:16.799 --> 00:03:17.749
As soon as I hit a goal,

00:03:17.749 --> 00:03:18.774
I'm on to the next thing.

00:03:18.774 --> 00:03:20.848
I don't take time to celebrate because

00:03:20.848 --> 00:03:23.226
the work is the celebration for me.

00:03:23.226 --> 00:03:24.197
I want to work more.

00:03:24.197 --> 00:03:25.030
I want to get better.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.678
I want to continue to improve.

00:03:26.678 --> 00:03:28.753
Hitting a goal and then
saying, "That's it"

00:03:28.753 --> 00:03:30.720
is death for me.

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:32.289
For a lot of people, when you hit a goal,

00:03:32.289 --> 00:03:34.227
it actually is depressing.

00:03:34.227 --> 00:03:35.837
When I sold my first business,

00:03:35.837 --> 00:03:37.457
I was 22 years old.

00:03:37.457 --> 00:03:38.330
It was a great high.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:39.503
Great, I sold the company,

00:03:39.503 --> 00:03:41.504
but then the next day I had nothing to do.

00:03:41.504 --> 00:03:42.476
"What do I,

00:03:42.476 --> 00:03:43.843
"what am I supposed to do?

00:03:43.843 --> 00:03:45.935
"I have nothing to go to in the morning."

00:03:45.935 --> 00:03:47.586
That's a great problem to have.

00:03:47.586 --> 00:03:49.138
It's not something I'm complaining about

00:03:49.138 --> 00:03:50.314
but it's still a problem.

00:03:50.314 --> 00:03:51.357
When you hit a goal

00:03:51.357 --> 00:03:53.501
and you don't know what
you're going to do next,

00:03:53.501 --> 00:03:54.857
it's depressing.

00:03:54.857 --> 00:03:56.962
You don't know what to do every day.

00:03:56.962 --> 00:03:59.546
When you don't have a plan
for what to do every day,

00:03:59.546 --> 00:04:01.528
it can really drag you down.

00:04:01.528 --> 00:04:03.586
I think in doing all these profiles

00:04:03.586 --> 00:04:05.441
of different famous entrepreneurs,

00:04:05.441 --> 00:04:07.510
people who've had massive success,

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:09.897
yes, it can be great to have a big goal.

00:04:09.897 --> 00:04:11.458
It can be great to win an award or

00:04:11.458 --> 00:04:13.093
hit a revenue target or

00:04:13.093 --> 00:04:15.360
land that big customer or whatever it is.

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:18.716
Go IPO, sell your company,
have some big goal,

00:04:18.716 --> 00:04:21.939
but if the goal is the only
thing that's driving you,

00:04:21.939 --> 00:04:23.793
it's going to be really hard to make it.

00:04:23.793 --> 00:04:25.936
With the most successful people,

00:04:25.936 --> 00:04:28.103
the journey is the reward.

00:04:29.536 --> 00:04:32.465
The journey of creating
something and marketing it

00:04:32.465 --> 00:04:35.529
and you getting better at
it and seeing the impact,

00:04:35.529 --> 00:04:36.834
that is the work.

00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:37.723
That is the goal.

00:04:37.723 --> 00:04:38.815
That is the joy.

00:04:38.815 --> 00:04:39.996
That is the excitement.

00:04:39.996 --> 00:04:43.188
That is where you derive
your most pleasure from,

00:04:43.188 --> 00:04:46.149
not just about hitting some target.

00:04:46.149 --> 00:04:47.939
I really challenge you to look at

00:04:47.939 --> 00:04:49.415
your life, your business.

00:04:49.415 --> 00:04:51.677
Think about what your goals are.

00:04:51.677 --> 00:04:54.431
I love setting goals
because when you set a goal,

00:04:54.431 --> 00:04:56.054
for me, the most important part of it

00:04:56.054 --> 00:04:58.746
is that it starts to align your actions

00:04:58.746 --> 00:05:00.516
to achieve that goal.

00:05:00.516 --> 00:05:02.031
It's not just about hitting the goal.

00:05:02.031 --> 00:05:03.756
It's about those actions.

00:05:03.756 --> 00:05:06.128
Those actions are what's going to serve me

00:05:06.128 --> 00:05:07.811
to be the best version of me,

00:05:07.811 --> 00:05:09.514
to allow me to have the big impact

00:05:09.514 --> 00:05:11.426
that I want to have.

00:05:11.426 --> 00:05:12.486
Look at your schedule.

00:05:12.486 --> 00:05:13.583
Look at what you're doing every day.

00:05:13.583 --> 00:05:15.261
Look at your day in, day out,

00:05:15.261 --> 00:05:17.093
in your business and in your life.

00:05:17.093 --> 00:05:18.093
Do you enjoy

00:05:19.137 --> 00:05:20.600
the journey?

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:21.608
For me,

00:05:21.608 --> 00:05:23.756
getting married, as an example,

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:25.694
I didn't really care
about the wedding day.

00:05:25.694 --> 00:05:27.408
Nina may not be too happy about that,

00:05:27.408 --> 00:05:28.641
but she knows.

00:05:28.641 --> 00:05:29.474
I didn't really care about the wedding.

00:05:29.474 --> 00:05:30.464
It's just another day.

00:05:30.464 --> 00:05:31.546
For me,

00:05:31.546 --> 00:05:32.700
the excitement,

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:33.749
the energy,

00:05:33.749 --> 00:05:36.556
the joy is in the marriage.

00:05:36.556 --> 00:05:37.878
It's the everyday.

00:05:37.878 --> 00:05:39.235
It's the journey,

00:05:39.235 --> 00:05:41.235
not just one day, right?

00:05:42.343 --> 00:05:44.840
When you have a kid, it's not just about

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:45.785
the kid being born.

00:05:45.785 --> 00:05:49.448
Having a goal to have
a kid, great, amazing.

00:05:49.448 --> 00:05:52.080
I have Hayden, almost eight years old.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.549
That was an amazing day,

00:05:53.549 --> 00:05:54.859
but it's the journey.

00:05:54.859 --> 00:05:55.711
It's the day-to-day.

00:05:55.711 --> 00:05:57.180
It's the parenting.

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:59.484
It's everyday, connecting.

00:05:59.484 --> 00:06:01.228
That's where you grow,

00:06:01.228 --> 00:06:03.131
and that's what you need to enjoy.

00:06:03.131 --> 00:06:04.849
If all you're waiting for as a parent

00:06:04.849 --> 00:06:07.225
is for your kid to move out,

00:06:07.225 --> 00:06:09.415
go to college, get a job,

00:06:09.415 --> 00:06:10.716
if all you're waiting for in your marriage

00:06:10.716 --> 00:06:14.029
is to hit that 10-year
anniversary or 25-year anniversary

00:06:14.029 --> 00:06:16.014
or two-year anniversary or whatever it is,

00:06:16.014 --> 00:06:17.535
you're missing out.

00:06:17.535 --> 00:06:19.994
The goal is not as important

00:06:19.994 --> 00:06:22.240
as the process to get there.

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:25.215
The goal helps you align
yourself so your actions

00:06:25.215 --> 00:06:27.461
help you be the best version of you.

00:06:27.461 --> 00:06:28.692
I'm not the guy who says, "No goals."

00:06:28.692 --> 00:06:29.525
Goals are important.

00:06:29.525 --> 00:06:30.449
I love having goals.

00:06:30.449 --> 00:06:32.277
I set goals for myself all the time,

00:06:32.277 --> 00:06:34.754
but much more important than the goal

00:06:34.754 --> 00:06:35.715
is the journey.

00:06:35.715 --> 00:06:36.548
The question of the day,

00:06:36.548 --> 00:06:37.684
I love your input.

00:06:37.684 --> 00:06:39.017
What do you guys think?

00:06:39.017 --> 00:06:40.109
Is the goal more important?

00:06:40.109 --> 00:06:41.578
Is the journey more important?

00:06:41.578 --> 00:06:42.543
Share your thoughts.

00:06:42.543 --> 00:06:43.647
Give some more context.

00:06:43.647 --> 00:06:45.339
I love to hear what's on your mind.

00:06:45.339 --> 00:06:46.494
Share it down in the comments below,

00:06:46.494 --> 00:06:48.421
and we'll join in the conversation.

00:06:48.421 --> 00:06:50.431
I also want to give a quick
shout-out to Gord Isman.

00:06:50.431 --> 00:06:52.092
Gord, thank you so much for picking up

00:06:52.092 --> 00:06:54.084
a copy of my book Your One Word.

00:06:54.084 --> 00:06:56.309
It really, really, really,
really means a lot to me,

00:06:56.309 --> 00:06:57.893
and I hope you're enjoying it.

00:06:57.893 --> 00:06:59.408
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:06:59.408 --> 00:07:00.524
I believe in you.

00:07:00.524 --> 00:07:02.493
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:07:02.493 --> 00:07:04.364
and whatever your One Word is,

00:07:04.364 --> 00:07:05.693
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:07:05.693 --> 00:07:07.004
for another shot

00:07:07.004 --> 00:07:08.065
of espresso.

00:07:08.065 --> 00:07:10.614
♫ I wake up every morning

00:07:10.614 --> 00:07:14.023
♫ Espresso keep me going

